# Datasets are never committed.
# The phishing feed contains live malicious URLs -- committing it will get
# the repo flagged by GitHub malware scanning and by corporate proxies.
data/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Scheduled-job output
logs/

# Trained model files. Regenerate them, don't version them -- EXCEPT the
# NumPy export, which is the thing the CLI actually loads. At 240 KB it is
# small enough to ship, and without it a fresh clone cannot run the headline
# command without first installing torch and retraining, which contradicts
# the README's whole "no PyTorch required" claim.
#
# Note the form: `models/` would exclude the directory outright and git will
# not descend into an excluded directory, so a later negation could never
# re-include a file inside it. `models/*` excludes the contents instead,
# which leaves the negation able to work.
*.pkl
*.pt
models/*
!models/cnn_numpy.npz

# Colab upload bundles. These repackage data/ (which is gitignored) into a
# zip at the repo root, where the data/ rule no longer covers it.
*-colab.zip

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Internal working notes -- not for publication
HANDOFF.md
